From f9d1e1069650ca90045abedbd83dfda2471f89a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 05:27:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] parse: a macro invoked by path in pattern position

tokio 1.53.1 `select!` (interprocess 2.4.4 os/unix/uds_local_socket/
tokio/stream.rs:52, skim 5.7.3):

    MACRO<tokio::select> error:0: Unexpected token TOK_EXCLAM, expected TOK_FATARROW

The final `select!` rule emits match arms whose patterns are macro
invocations by path: `$crate::count!( $($skip)* ) => { .. }` and
`$crate::select_priv_clean_pattern!($bind) => {}`. Parse_Pattern1 only
recognised the `ident!(..)` form. A path-shaped pattern went through
Parse_PatternReal_Path, which knows `(`, `{` or a plain value and then
stopped at the `!`. Every crate that invokes `tokio::select!` hit
this; tokio itself only defines the macro.

Parse_PatternReal_Path now parses `path!(..)` as a macro pattern, as
type position (Parse_Type_Path) already does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/src/parse/pattern.cpp b/src/parse/pattern.cpp
index 87dd01e0..c08d4916 100644
--- a/src/parse/pattern.cpp
+++ b/src/parse/pattern.cpp
@@ -378,6 +378,10 @@ AST::Pattern Parse_PatternReal_Path(TokenStream& lex, ProtoSpan ps, AST::Path pa
         return AST::Pattern( AST::Pattern::TagNamedTuple(), lex.end_span(ps), mv$(path), Parse_PatternTuple(lex, nullptr) );
     case TOK_BRACE_OPEN:
         return Parse_PatternStruct(lex, ps, mv$(path));
+    // A macro invoked by path, as `Parse_Pattern1` handles `ident!(..)`
+    // - tokio 1.53.1 `select!`: its match arms are `$crate::count!( $($skip)* ) => ..` (interprocess 2.4.4, skim)
+    case TOK_EXCLAM:
+        return AST::Pattern( AST::Pattern::TagMacro(), lex.end_span(ps), box$(Parse_MacroInvocation(ps, mv$(path), lex)) );
     default:
         PUTBACK(tok, lex);
         return AST::Pattern( AST::Pattern::TagValue(), lex.end_span(ps), AST::Pattern::Value::make_Named(mv$(path)) );
